# Nothing is mounted from this file.
#
# This file exists only to override the one NVIDIA writes. The nvidia-l4t-init
# package's post-installation script replaces /etc/fstab whenever it sees the
# flag file in /opt/nvidia/l4t-packages that this build uses to stop the
# bootloader package from flashing firmware. The file it writes contains:
#
#   /dev/root  /  ext4  defaults  0 1
#
# That line is right for a Jetson installed NVIDIA's way, where the initramfs
# creates a /dev/root device node. This image does not: the root filesystem is
# named on the kernel command line by its partition identifier, and the
# initramfs mounts it before anything reads this file. Leaving NVIDIA's version
# in place would leave systemd with a mount unit pointing at a device that does
# not exist.
#
# Everything else that needs mounting is handled by systemd. /tmp comes from
# tmp.mount, and the EFI system partition is picked up automatically by
# systemd-gpt-auto-generator, which finds it on the disk the firmware booted
# from.
